the US dollar has a pretty privileged  position among world currencies which is  good for the United States because it's  a trading currency it's a reserve  currency in many parts of the world so  it's not just within the United States  that the dollar is used it's used by  countries all over the world for  transactions between many other  countries forty to forty five percent of  international payments happen in dollars  two-thirds of global reserves are in  dollars two-thirds of physical dollar  bills are outside of the United States  this global reliance on the dollar keeps  interest rates low which is good for our  economy it's really easy to sell US  bonds because a lot of the world is  already operating in dollars and trading  with other countries meaning imports and  exports trading with other countries is  one step easier for the United States  because our currency happens to be one  that's already being used by many other  countries but the consequences would be  bigger than just these numbers if the  United States dollar were no longer such  a prominent currency we have clout  economically around the world and  diplomatically around the world because  of the prevalence of our currency being  used by different countries the world  wants dollars which makes American  exports worth more this is where we get  to the current administration  unfortunately under Donald Trump under  this increased geopolitical economic  diplomatic instability that a surfaced  under Trump we're seeing the world start  to move away from u.s. dollars more and  more and it is really important to  understand this we might feel as though  obviously the dollar is the currency of  the world  it's nothing fixed or immutable about  that it might seem like dollars are at  the top of the food chain but the reason  for that is a lot of what I've told you  and the fact that the US has been seen  as a sort of stable geopolitical player  that can be trusted to stick to our  agreements to be present in our  alliances that's increasingly in  question and there are two sort of  unrelated ways in which Donald Trump is  causing the self-inflicted demise of the  dollar number one is that the status of  the u.s. around the world as  untrustworthy hurts our credibility this  includes Trump backing out of agreements  for no good reason  this includes you know the Iran deal the  Paris climate deal that's the sort of  geopolitical attack on the dollar that  we're seeing  then there's the economic one trumps  tariffs for example buy by virtue of how  they impact our allies push other  countries to say maybe maybe we don't  want to be dealing in the dollar the  dollar starts to become a risk for other  countries to hold rather than a stable  mechanism and then we get to one of the  most interesting aspects of this Donald  Trump has been talking about how the  trade deficit is really a bad thing  meaning when we have a trade deficit we  are importing more than we are exporting  or we are buying more than we're selling  we're consuming more than we are  producing what that means is that we  have to borrow at the country level to  pay for a lot of that stuff that we're  consuming that means more dollars are  going out than dollars coming in that's  why there are all these dollars floating  around the world that other countries  use for transactions and make it easier  for them to use the dollar as their  reserve currency if Trump succeeds in  getting rid of our trade deficit the  number of extra dollars around the world  goes way down which hurts our clout as a  reserve currency basic economics and  very quickly this starts to get into way  more sort of advanced economics then  certainly Trump can understand but the  point is that the same trade deficit  that Donald Trump claims to want to get  rid of to help the United States would  actually be even more damaging to the US  dollar if he did it he claims to be a  nationalist that's his word if  that's the case why is he advocating a  policy that would be bad for the US  dollar the national currency which I  would imagine nationalists would want to  support send me your thoughts on that  we're going to talk more about it on  upcoming programs
 

